  "description": "Marketing is a broad business discipline that includes advertising, branding, sales, digital media, product development, pricing, distribution, and market research all working together to create a comprehensive marketing strategy. Marketers seek to understand their customers in order to deliver goods and services in a way that brings them the most value. Learn how this can be done in ways that glorify God and promote human flourishing. The BA in marketing is offered in three concentrations: Analytics and Research: Learn research and data analytics techniques needed to understand consumers, culture and the business environment to enable the creation of marketing strategies. Marketing Management: Learn how to develop strategies and implement marketing programs to create value for an organization and the consumers they serve. Professional Selling: Learn the skills of relationship selling and caring for customers. Overlap Policy This program may not be combined with another marketing concentration or the business minor program. No more than two majors from the School of Business may be obtained.",
